spans.s:
मू॑ल n. (adj. —˚ f. आ & ई) root (lit. & fig.), foot,
basis, foundation, ground, bottom, immediate neighbourhood^1;
 origin,
source
[]
commencement, cause;
 the chief person or thing, e.g. text
(opp. commentary), capital (opp. interest), also capital = chief city,
holder (opp. owner);
 N. of a lunar mansion (also m.). — मूलं कृ or
बन्ध् take root;
 मूल (—˚) sprung from, rooted in, resting on;
(˚—) original, chief, first, also = (±आ) मूलात् or मूलतस् &
मूलादारभ्य from the bottom or the beginning.
[1] Correction submitted by AnnaRybakovaT, Jim Funderburk. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/25.

मूलक f. ˚लिका = prec. (—˚);
 n. an esculent root,
radish.

मूलफल n. sgl. roots and fruits;
 the interests of
